Tiffin, PayLane and the people named in the scenarios are fictional. Every user name, password and
client secret in this repository belongs to containers on a developer's machine and to nothing else.

The sample builds on MP Core and, through it, on these open-source projects, each under its own licence:
Wolverine and JasperFx (MIT), Entity Framework Core and ASP.NET Core (MIT), Npgsql (PostgreSQL Licence),
FluentValidation (Apache-2.0), OpenTelemetry .NET (Apache-2.0), Polly (BSD-3-Clause), gRPC for .NET
(Apache-2.0), StackExchange.Redis (MIT), Confluent.Kafka (Apache-2.0), RabbitMQ .NET client
(Apache-2.0 / MPL-2.0), the AWS SDK for .NET (Apache-2.0). Its tests use xUnit (Apache-2.0) and NetArchTest (MIT).

The containers it starts are the official images of PostgreSQL, TimescaleDB, Apache Kafka, RabbitMQ,
Redis, Keycloak, Apache APISIX, RustFS, SeaweedFS, WireMock, the OpenTelemetry Collector, Jaeger, Prometheus
and Grafana, each under its own licence. None of them is distributed with this repository.

